   "Northwind-negotiator": "compromising",
   "Halcyon-researcher": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "competing",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "compromising"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "S1 is essentially the safe version: 24-hour serious reporting, all other incidents within five business days (~7 days), customer notice in 72 hours, and all-incident scope. S2 keeps the 5% permanent limit and 55 °C test but lets a model above 5% stay on sale through a 90-day corrective window with no interim cap, and per-model results go to purchasers (not the general public), satisfying both disclosure red lines. S3 honours NW-2 with a 6-year retrofit (plus 'where technically feasible') but its 24-month new-unit deadline is looser than the acceptable band, while S5 has no mandatory numeric recall (8/100k only triggers review, notice and a corrective plan, with recall left to the regulator), which is a clear win for Halcyon's Ember 8."
 },
